---
// Sampath › 07 — Delivery: two surprises along the way. The Spine / Lottie / Rive decision
// (three option cards, then two paragraphs side by side), a rule, then the bank-staff testing
// findings (Figma's card borders and footnote removed by the user).
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Section from './Section.astro';
import spineLogo from '../../assets/images/sampath/25_07-delivery__image-186.png';
import lottieLogo from '../../assets/images/sampath/26_07-delivery__image-186.png';
import riveLogo from '../../assets/images/sampath/27_07-delivery__image-186.png';

// `inset` logos sit 39 × 38 inside the tile (Spine); the others fill it. `outlined` adds the
// warm border Figma gives the Rive tile.
const options = [
  {
    logo: spineLogo,
    inset: true,
    name: 'Spine',
    tagline: '2D animation · game-focused',
    text: 'Keep Spine. Devs swap their package. Higher quality, adds implementation risk.',
  },
  {
    logo: lottieLogo,
    chosen: true,
    name: 'Lottie',
    tagline: 'JSON-based animation · web and app',
    text: 'Rebuild in Lottie. Devs keep their existing package. Minimal risk, fits the timeline.',
  },
  {
    logo: riveLogo,
    outlined: true,
    name: 'Rive',
    tagline: 'Interactive animation · state machine',
    text: 'More capable for app-level animation. A new package and new learning for the team.',
  },
];

const findings = [
  {
    status: 'Clear to users',
    tone: 'positive',
    title: 'Quick actions carousel was understood immediately',
    text: 'The micro interaction showing horizontal scroll was enough. Users engaged with the carousel without prompting and navigated it confidently.',
  },
  {
    status: 'Not noticed',
    tone: 'caution',
    title: 'Account carousel was not seen as swipeable',
    text: "The section showing accounts, FDs, and loans had no scroll affordance. Users didn't attempt to swipe. Reusing the quick actions micro-interaction would only feel repetitive, so we started exploring a different way to show it scrolls.",
  },
  {
    status: 'Not noticed',
    tone: 'caution',
    title: "Card details page entry point wasn't visible",
    text: "On the credit and debit card pages, users didn't realise tapping the card would open the details and transaction history. No call to action to communicate it was interactive.",
  },
];
---

<Section tone="warm" labelledby="delivery-title">
  <!-- The right fix for now, the right tool for next -->
  <div class="part">
    <div class="intro">
      <h2 id="delivery-title">
        <span class="line">Two surprises</span>{' '}
        <span class="line">along the way.</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="sub">
        <h3 class="text-h6">The right fix for now, the right tool for next</h3>
        <p class="text-body-l body">
          Developers started building halfway through the UI phase, and the first thing that
          broke was the animations. Our animator had made them in Spine, but the developers were
          using the Lottie package, and the illustrations simply wouldn’t render. For a while,
          none of us could work out why. So I took a screenshot of the error and gave it to
          Claude. It came back with the cause and three ways forward, which gave the team
          something concrete to decide on.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ul class="cards" role="list">
      {options.map(({ logo, inset, outlined, chosen, name, tagline, text }) => (
        <li class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <span class:list={['logo', { inset, outlined }]}>
              <Image src={logo} alt="" widths={[44, 88]} sizes="44px" />
            </span>
            {chosen && <span class="chosen text-label-xs">Chosen</span>}
          </div>
          <div class="card-name">
            <h4 class="text-title-l">{name}</h4>
            <p class="text-title-s tagline">{tagline}</p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-body-m body">{text}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="cols text-body-l body">
      <p>
        My pick was Rive. It handles complex, interactive animation at a fraction of the weight,
        and the gamification features coming in phase 2 will need exactly that. But switching
        packages mid-build meant new R&amp;D with the deadline fixed, and the risk wasn't worth it
        for phase 1.
      </p>
      <p>
        So we split the decision. Lottie now, to ship on time. Rive for phase 2, which I made the
        case for with our PO, and they agreed. Lottie solved the problem for now, and Rive is
        ready for what comes next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr />

  <!-- Testing with bank staff -->
  <div class="part">
    <div class="sub">
      <h3 class="text-h6">Testing with bank staff</h3>
      <p class="text-body-l body">
        The real build was still in its early stages in code, but the main flows needed testing
        before it caught up. So our design team built a working prototype with Claude Code in a
        few hours. We then put it in front of 15 bank staff and watched them work through the main
        flows on their own. Getting there that fast meant we could run a real session long before
        the final build was ready. The reactions were genuine. It wasn’t a formal study, but it
        came early enough that what it surfaced could actually be acted on.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="cards" role="list">
      {findings.map(({ status, tone, title, text }) => (
        <li class="card">
          <span class:list={['pill text-label-s', tone]}>{status}</span>
          <h4 class="text-title-l">{title}</h4>
          <p class="text-body-m body">{text}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  /* ── Parts: intro, cards and paragraphs 40 apart ───────────────── */

  .part {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-40);
  }

  .intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
  }

  h2,
  h3,
  h4 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  /* Two lines from tablet up, as in Figma; on mobile it wraps naturally. */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .line {
      display: block;
    }
  }

  .sub {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .sub .body {
    max-width: 500px;
  }

  .body {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Figma gap 28; 24 to match the paragraph pairs in 06. */
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-24);
  }

  hr {
    margin-block: var(--space-56);
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sampath-border-warm);
  }

  /* ── Cards: three across from tablet up. Figma gap 10, snapped to 8. ── */

  .cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .cards {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    padding: var(--space-16);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background-color: var(--bg-cards);
  }

  .card-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-self: stretch;
  }

  .logo {
    display: grid;
    flex: none;
    place-items: center;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--sampath-logo-tile);
  }

  .logo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .logo.inset img {
    width: 39px;
    height: 38px;
  }

  .logo.outlined {
    border: 1px solid var(--sampath-border-warm);
  }

  /* Figma: Inter 10 Medium, padding 8/3; site font at label-xs, padding snapped to 8/4. */
  .chosen {
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background-color: var(--fg-sampath-blue);
    color: var(--text-white);
  }

  .card-name {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .tagline {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  /* Same size as the 01 Starting Point badges: label-s, padding 4/8 (user; Figma was Inter 12,
     padding 12/8). */
  .pill {
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  }

  /* Same colours as the "Chosen" badge (user; Figma was green). */
  .pill.positive {
    background-color: var(--fg-sampath-blue);
    color: var(--text-white);
  }

  .pill.caution {
    background-color: var(--sampath-pill-caution-bg);
    color: var(--sampath-pill-caution-text);
  }

  /* ── Mobile: 32 either side of the rule, as in 04 and 06; paragraphs stacked 16 apart ── */

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    hr {
      margin-block: var(--space-32);
    }

    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-16);
    }
  }
</style>
